BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gainssa-ai-safety-essentials-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Deadline: GAIN SSA: AI Safety Essentials Fellowship (inaugural coho
 rt)
DESCRIPTION:GAIN SSA (Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa) runs th
 e AI Safety Essentials Fellowship for residents of Africa considering how 
 they can be effective contributors in shaping the continent's transition t
 oward containing risks from transformative AI. Fellows spend six weeks map
 ping the priorities and gaps that need to be filled in Africa's AI safety 
 ecosystem\, through curated pre-reading and a live group call each week (a
 bout 5 hours per week). CURRICULUM: existential risks and catastrophic vec
 tors\; frontier AI models and Africa\; defining safe and beneficial AI\; s
 ubfields and alignment architectures\; Africa's AI safety landscape and po
 licy\; and a capstone week on fellowships and career launch\, with guidanc
 e toward international pipelines such as MATS\, ERA\, BlueDot and GovAI. M
 entorship comes from international AI safety researchers\, governance fell
 ows and peer builders. FUNDING: after the program\, top capstone action-pl
 an proposals are funded from a USD 500 to 1\,000 micro-grant pool (capped 
 at USD 1\,000)\, including proposals needing compute\, travel to AI alignm
 ent conferences in Sub-Saharan Africa\, or communication work (for example
  Substack Pro for writers)\; results are shared within 10 days of receivin
 g a proposal. The main aim is to have participants take action to build Af
 rica's first AI safety systems. APPLICATION: expression of interest for th
 e inaugural cohort via the Google Form linked from the program page. DEADL
 INE: expressions of interest close 8 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: GAIN 
 SSA (Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa)\nLocation: Online (virt
 ual\, facilitated). Open to residents of African countries.\nAward: Micro-
 grant pool funding top capstone proposals at USD 500 to 1\,000 each (cappe
 d at USD 1\,000)\, usable for compute access\, communication work such as 
 Substack Pro subscriptions for writers\, or travel to AI alignment confere
 nces in Sub-Saharan Africa. The fellowship itself is free to attend (no pa
 rticipation fee\, no application fee)\; no stipend is paid during the prog
 ram.\nDuration: 6-week facilitated virtual curriculum plus an onboarding p
 re-requisites module (the site also describes it as 7 weeks)\, about 5 hou
 rs per week with one live group call per week\; capstone proposals are fun
 ded afterwards\, with results within 10 days of submission.\n\nMore: https
 ://gainssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://gainssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (virtual\, facilitated). Open to residents of African count
 ries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Fellowship 2027-2028 for Artists\, Scholars and T
 hinkers (Cassis\, France)
DESCRIPTION:The Camargo Foundation invites artists\, scholars and thinkers 
 to its flagship Core Fellowship: a ten-week self-directed residency on its
  clifftop campus overlooking the Mediterranean in Cassis\, France\, dedica
 ted to research\, experimentation and interdisciplinary exchange. Curators
  apply under the Thinkers category\, which covers accomplished professiona
 ls and practitioners in cultural and creative fields who are professionall
 y engaged in critical thought\, including curators\, critics and journalis
 ts\; projects should engage theoretical\, artistic or societal questions. 
 WHAT YOU GET: a stipend of EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 total)\, basic tra
 nsportation funding\, and a furnished apartment with an equipped kitchen o
 n campus. Fourteen fellowships are awarded per year: seven for artists and
  seven for scholars and thinkers. RESIDENCY PERIODS: Fall 2027 (8 Septembe
 r to 17 November 2027) or Spring 2028 (23 February to 4 May 2028). ELIGIBI
 LITY: artists in visual arts\, performance\, writing\, film\, music or mul
 tidisciplinary work with at least 5 years of professional practice\; schol
 ars holding or pursuing a PhD focused on French and Francophone cultures o
 r cross-cultural Mediterranean studies\; and thinkers as described above. 
 APPLICATION: via Submittable with a 100-word proposal summary\, a 1\,200-w
 ord proposal narrative\, a 300-word rationale for Camargo\, a 300-word car
 eer-stage rationale\, a CV (max 3 pages)\, work samples and two references
 . NOTE: the foundation has announced that this is the final Fellowship sel
 ected through a public open call until further notice\; a new selection pr
 ocess begins in July 2027\, making this the last chance to apply directly.
 \n\nOrganisation: Camargo Foundation\nLocation: Camargo Foundation campus\
 , Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.\nAward: EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 to
 tal for the ten-week residency)\, plus basic travel funding and a furnishe
 d apartment with equipped kitchen on the Camargo campus. 14 fellowships pe
 r year: 7 for artists and 7 for scholars and thinkers. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Ten weeks\, either 8 September to 17 November 2027 or 23 Febru
 ary to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fello
 wship-2026-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Camargo Foundation campus\, Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:braunschweig-projects-curatorial-fellowship-2027-28@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Braunschweig Projects 2027/28: Curatorial Fellowship at H
 BK Braunschweig
DESCRIPTION:The curatorial strand of the Braunschweig Projects fellowship p
 rogramme at Braunschweig University of Art (HBK Braunschweig)\, funded by 
 the State of Lower Saxony\, offers one curator a twelve-month fellowship b
 eginning 1 April 2027. The fellow develops a curatorial concept culminatin
 g in a final exhibition and presentation in January/February 2028\; projec
 ts should ideally connect to a museum\, collection or cultural institution
  in Lower Saxony. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 1\,600 per month for twelve months\, a
  rent-free studio apartment designed for one person (with a EUR 250 monthl
 y contribution towards incidental living costs charged to the fellow)\, a 
 subsidy of up to EUR 4\,000 to support exhibition activities and a EUR 2\,
 000 travel budget. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must have gained initial curato
 rial experience of at least three years\; no formal degree is specified. F
 ellows may not hold regular income from third parties or other state fundi
 ng during the fellowship\, and must spend at least eight months of the HBK
  lecture period on site in Braunschweig. Participation in the Welcome Week
 s (19 to 30 April 2027) and the final presentation is mandatory. APPLICATI
 ON: submit a project draft covering research\, preparation\, implementatio
 n\, budget and communication plans via the HBK application portal. DEADLIN
 E: 4 October 2026\, 23:59. The artistic fellowships strand (fine arts and 
 sound art) runs in parallel with the same deadline.\n\nOrganisation: Braun
 schweig University of Art (HBK Braunschweig)\, on behalf of the State of L
 ower Saxony\nLocation: Braunschweig\, Germany. Open worldwide\; at least e
 ight months of the HBK lecture period must be spent on site.\nAward: Stipe
 nd of EUR 1\,600 per month for 12 months (EUR 19\,200 total)\, plus a rent
 -free one-person studio apartment in Braunschweig (the fellow pays EUR 250
  per month towards incidental living costs)\, a subsidy of up to EUR 4\,00
 0 for exhibition activities and a EUR 2\,000 travel budget. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Twelve months from 1 April 2027\, with a final presentati
 on in January/February 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.hbk-bs.de/hochschule/sti
 pendienprogramme/braunschweig-projects-kuratorinnen-stipendium/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hbk-bs.de/hochschule/stipendienprogramme/braunschweig-proje
 cts-kuratorinnen-stipendium/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Braunschweig\, Germany. Open worldwide\; at least eight months of 
 the HBK lecture period must be spent on site.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asymmetry-assistant-curator-fellowship-nottingham-2027@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asymmetry Assistant Curator Fellowship 2027-2029 at Notti
 ngham Contemporary
DESCRIPTION:Asymmetry Art Foundation and Nottingham Contemporary offer a fu
 lly funded two-year Assistant Curator Fellowship embedded in the curatoria
 l team of one of Europe's leading contemporary art institutions. The fello
 wship is geared towards an early-career curator who\, to any extent\, iden
 tifies with Chinese or Sinophone cultures or backgrounds\, continuing Asym
 metry's programme of curatorial fellowships at UK institutions (previous p
 lacements include Chisenhale Gallery and Whitechapel Gallery). WHAT YOU DO
 : contribute to exhibitions\, artist commissions\, live programmes\, resea
 rch\, writing and institutional development\, working across all stages of
  projects while developing independent curatorial work and joining Asymmet
 ry's international network of scholars and practitioners. WHAT YOU GET: an
  annual salary of GBP 27\,556 plus pension and National Insurance contribu
 tions\, annual leave plus UK bank holidays\, visa and legal fee assistance
  where required\, and a travel and relocation allowance. ELIGIBILITY: earl
 y-career curators with roughly 1 to 3 years of experience\, an educational
  background in art history\, cultural studies or related fields\, familiar
 ity with contemporary artistic practices\, direct experience collaborating
  with artists\, and proficiency in English. Applications must be in Englis
 h\; accessibility support is available via fellowship@asymmetryart.org. AP
 PLICATION: via the Asymmetry application portal. DEADLINE: 25 October 2026
 . The fellowship runs 6 April 2027 to 5 April 2029.\n\nOrganisation: Asymm
 etry Art Foundation\, with Nottingham Contemporary\nLocation: Nottingham C
 ontemporary\, Nottingham\, UK. Open internationally to early-career curato
 rs who identify with Chinese or Sinophone cultures or backgrounds\; visa a
 nd relocation support provided.\nAward: Annual salary of GBP 27\,556 for t
 wo years\, plus pension and National Insurance contributions\, annual leav
 e in line with organisational policy plus UK bank holidays\, visa and lega
 l fee assistance where required\, and a travel and relocation allowance. N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Two years\, 6 April 2027 to 5 April 2029.\n\
 nMore: https://www.asymmetryart.org/fellowships/open-calls/2027-asymmetry-
 assistant-curator-fellowship-nottingham-contemporary-opencall?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asymmetryart.org/fellowships/open-calls/2027-asymmetry-assi
 stant-curator-fellowship-nottingham-contemporary-opencall?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nottingham Contemporary\, Nottingham\, UK. Open internationally to
  early-career curators who identify with Chinese or Sinophone cultures or 
 backgrounds\; visa and relocation support provided.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iaps-ai-policy-fellowship-spring-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: IAPS: AI Policy Fellowship Spring 2027 (DC\, London or re
 mote)
DESCRIPTION:The Institute for AI Policy and Strategy (IAPS) runs a three-mo
 nth\, fully funded AI policy fellowship placing fellows on concrete AI gov
 ernance and policy research projects. Spring 2027 cohort: 22 February to 1
 4 May 2027\, opening with a mandatory in-person component in Washington DC
  from 22 February to 5 March 2027\, after which fellows work from the DC o
 ffice\, the London office or remotely. STIPENDS: USD 18\,000 for Fellows a
 nd USD 24\,000 for Senior Fellows\, plus USD 3\,000 extra on the in-person
  DC or London tracks\, healthcare benefits and a USD 500 professional deve
 lopment stipend. ELIGIBILITY: no technical background or prior policy expe
 rience required\; the DC track requires the right to work in the US betwee
 n 22 February and 14 May 2027\, and no visa sponsorship is available for t
 he US or UK\; the remote track is open globally with country-specific exce
 ptions. TIMELINE: initial responses mid-October 2026\, live interviews in 
 November\, final selections early December. Deadline 27 September 2026. Ap
 ply at https://www.guidedtrack.com/programs/ll4vpg7/run.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Institute for AI Policy and Strategy (IAPS)\nLocation: Washington DC or Lo
 ndon track (desk space provided)\, or fully remote from most countries. Ma
 ndatory in-person opening in Washington DC\, 22 February to 5 March 2027. 
 No visa sponsorship for the US or UK.\nAward: Fellows receive USD 18\,000 
 and Senior Fellows USD 24\,000 as a stipend for the three-month full-time 
 program\, plus an additional USD 3\,000 stipend on the in-person DC or Lon
 don tracks\, healthcare benefits and a USD 500 professional development st
 ipend. Up to 45 fellows. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months full-
 time\, 22 February to 14 May 2027\; extensions of 4 to 12 weeks were offer
 ed to more than half of the previous cohort\n\nMore: https://www.iaps.ai/f
 ellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.iaps.ai/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Washington DC or London track (desk space provided)\, or fully rem
 ote from most countries. Mandatory in-person opening in Washington DC\, 22
  February to 5 March 2027. No visa sponsorship for the US or UK.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-policy-press-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tech Policy Press Fellowship Program 2027
DESCRIPTION:Tech Policy Press is recruiting its 2027 fellowship cohort to p
 ursue independent reporting and analysis on urgent questions at the inters
 ection of technology and democracy. Since 2023 the programme has supported
  25 fellows from 11 countries across three cohorts\, writing on AI governa
 nce\, tech regulation\, digital rights and the entanglement of state and c
 orporate power. WHO IT IS FOR: mid-career journalists\, researchers\, lawy
 ers and public policy professionals with a strong background in a specific
  tech policy area\, a particular geography\, or technology's impact on dem
 ocracy and society. Applicants from the Global Majority and from communiti
 es underrepresented in media are encouraged\, as are projects that centre 
 communities and regions usually excluded from global tech policy conversat
 ions. Contributions can range from original reporting to policy analysis\,
  and technical practitioners are welcome as long as the work fits the publ
 ication's editorial purview. EXPECTATIONS: at least one piece of analysis 
 or reporting per month (exclusive to Tech Policy Press\, though it may be 
 republished elsewhere)\, a mandatory hour-long monthly cohort meeting\, a 
 monthly check-in with the editorial team\, collaboration with other fellow
 s and the masthead\, agreed deadlines\, and disclosure of conflicts of int
 erest. Applicants should arrive with a clear area of focus and a sense of 
 how the work will inform both the public and decision-makers. APPLY via th
 e online form by 11:59pm EDT on 24 September 2026\, with a CV or resume\, 
 a cover letter of no more than two pages\, links to prior publications (op
 en access\, published within the past three years\, at least one in Englis
 h and at least one solo-authored\; social posts\, pre-prints and unpublish
 ed coursework do not count) and two professional references. Shortlisted c
 andidates may be invited to an online interview. Decisions are expected by
  early December 2026. Two optional Zoom information sessions run on 9 Sept
 ember at 8am EDT and 16 September at 7pm EDT\; registration required.\n\nO
 rganisation: Tech Policy Press\nLocation: Fully remote\, worldwide. Intern
 ational applicants explicitly encouraged\; fellows work as independent con
 tractors. No requirement to be authorised to work in the USA.\nAward: USD 
 10\,000 stipend per fellow\, paid quarterly. Also included: editorial guid
 ance from the Tech Policy Press team\, membership of an international coho
 rt with regular feedback and exchange\, and monthly sessions to strengthen
  the work. Fellows' work is published on the Tech Policy Press website and
  promoted through the newsletter\, podcast and events. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Twelve months\, part-time\, running January to December 2027\n
 \nMore: https://www.techpolicy.press/call-for-applications-2027-tech-polic
 y-press-fellowship-program/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://www.techpolicy.press/call-for-applications-2027-tech-policy-pre
 ss-fellowship-program/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
LOCATION:Fully remote\, worldwide. International applicants explicitly enco
 uraged\; fellows work as independent contractors. No requirement to be aut
 horised to work in the USA.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sundance-episodic-program-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sundance Institute: Episodic Program and Lab 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Sundance Institute Episodic Program is an entry point for e
 merging to mid-career writers and creators working across all scripted ser
 ies platforms\, combining a lab experience with customised support to move
  projects and careers forward. The Episodic Lab lets writers workshop an o
 riginal pilot and develop their writing and pitching skills: working with 
 showrunners\, producers and executives\, fellows take part in one-on-one s
 tory meetings\, pitching sessions\, craft workshops and writers rooms. Up 
 to ten applicants are selected\, either for the in-person Lab (preceded by
  virtual workshops) or for a fully virtual Intensive with a creative advis
 or. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be 18 or older\; the script must be the a
 pplicant's original creation or adapted from optioned source material and 
 written in English\; the draft must be revised or new\, not already produc
 ed\, not sold to a third party and not distributed online\; and applicants
  cannot have previously had an episodic project (pilot or pitch) produced 
 by a studio or network. Open to international and U.S. participants\, subj
 ect to travel guidelines. Up to two writers per project may participate\, 
 with one named as primary applicant. APPLICATION: submitted via FilmFreewa
 y\, including writer bios (250 words each)\, a series logline (50 words)\,
  pilot synopsis (500 words)\, one-page series overview (500 words)\, perso
 nal statement (250 words)\, community connection\, thematic statement (250
  words)\, characters and core relationships (250 words)\, episodic vision\
 , optional video samples (up to three links\, 10 minutes total)\, and the 
 full pilot script as a PDF in standard screenplay format. Demographic ques
 tions are optional and do not affect consideration. Candidates may submit 
 up to three applications\, with a separate application and USD 50 fee for 
 each project. Submissions opened 13 July 2026 and close 25 August 2026 at 
 6:00 p.m. PT. Finalists are notified by email through FilmFreeway around m
 id to late March 2027 (FilmFreeway lists 31 March 2027)\, and the list of 
 selected writers and projects is published at sundance.org/epi after 15 Ap
 ril 2027. Finalists must return a Fellow Agreement\, a Participation Agree
 ment and any other required documents within five days. Questions: episodi
 cprogram@sundance.org.\n\nOrganisation: Sundance Institute\nLocation: Open
  to international and U.S. applicants. In-person Lab takes place in the At
 lanta\, Georgia area\, USA in Spring 2027\; the Intensive track is fully o
 nline.\nAward: No stipend or honorarium for participation. For the in-pers
 on Lab\, Sundance covers round-trip basic economy airfare from the airport
  nearest the fellow's residence\, shared housing with a private room and b
 ath\, and ground transport to and from the airport (fellows within 100 mil
 es of the Lab get ground transport only). Meals\, in-room charges\, travel
  insurance\, luggage fees and taxes are the fellow's own cost. One selecte
 d project also receives a separate monetary grant from the Alfred P. Sloan
  Foundation for a series with an illuminating emphasis on science\, includ
 ing medicine\, energy\, technology or invention. APPLICATION FEE: USD 50 n
 onrefundable processing fee per project submitted.\nDuration: In-person La
 b in Spring 2027 (event dates 15 to 20 April 2027) preceded by virtual wor
 kshops\; the Intensive track convenes virtually in Summer 2027.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://filmfreeway.com/SundanceEpisodicLab2027?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://filmfreeway.com/SundanceEpisodicLab2027?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open to international and U.S. applicants. In-person Lab takes pla
 ce in the Atlanta\, Georgia area\, USA in Spring 2027\; the Intensive trac
 k is fully online.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:instituto-sacatar-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: Instituto Sacatar: Sacatar Fellowship 2027 (Bahia\, Brazi
 l)
DESCRIPTION:Brazil's longest-running artist residency\, on the island of It
 aparica across the bay from Salvador\, hosting six to eight artists per se
 ssion for roughly eight weeks. Open to all creative disciplines and\, unus
 ually for this region\, to all nationalities\, which makes it one of the f
 ew genuinely international residencies in Latin America. Sacatar provides 
 full hosting (private room\, three meals daily\, individual studio\, laund
 ry\, local logistics and connections) but explicitly does NOT provide a st
 ipend\, airfare to Salvador\, art materials or discretionary local expense
 s\, so applicants must fund their own travel. Individual artists only\; gr
 oup proposals are not accepted and former Sacatar Fellows may not reapply.
  COVID vaccination is required. NOTE: there is a USD 25 application fee. A
 pply through SlideRoom by 28 August 2026. Contact info@sacatar.org.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Instituto Sacatar\nLocation: Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil.
  Open to all nationalities.\nAward: Fully hosted residency: private bedroo
 m with attached bathroom\, three meals a day (except Saturday evenings\, S
 undays and Brazilian holidays)\, an individual studio suited to the discip
 line\, weekly laundry\, logistical support and airport transfer from Salva
 dor. NO STIPEND\, no airfare and no materials budget. USD 25 application f
 ee. One French artist may additionally receive airfare and a stipend throu
 gh Villa Fatumbi.\nDuration: Approximately eight weeks\; specific session 
 dates are listed in the application.\n\nMore: https://sacatar.org/en/fello
 wships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sacatar.org/en/fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil. Open to all nationalities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
