SUMMARY:Deadline: FAS: AI Safety Policy Entrepreneurship Fellowship 2026-27
  (part-time\, remote)
DESCRIPTION:The Federation of American Scientists' AI Safety Policy Entrepr
 eneurship Fellowship helps early- to mid-career professionals advance a fr
 ontier-AI-safety policy idea from concept toward implementation as a FAS a
 ffiliate. Fellows get policy-entrepreneurship training\, reading groups\, 
 and twice-monthly check-ins while developing a policy memo and advocacy pl
 an\; the strongest receives a USD 1\,000 merit award on top of the USD 5\,
 000 stipend. ELIGIBILITY: subject-matter expertise from technical AI resea
 rch\, academia\, think tanks\, civil society\, industry\, law\, cybersecur
 ity\, or national security\, with limited prior policy experience\; the wo
 rk is primarily remote with two mandatory US in-person events (California 
 retreat 4-7 November 2026\, DC capstone week of 22 February 2027). Runs 30
  September 2026 to 28 February 2027 at about 5 hours per week. DEADLINE: 7
  September 2026\, 11:59PM ET.\n\nOrganisation: Federation of American Scie
 ntists (Day One Project)\nLocation: Primarily remote\, US-policy focused\,
  with two mandatory in-person events in the US (California retreat 4-7 Nov
 ember 2026\; Washington DC capstone the week of 22 February 2027).\nAward:
  USD 5\,000 stipend for the part-time fellowship (about 5 hours per week)\
 , plus a USD 1\,000 merit award for the most actionable policy memo and ad
 vocacy plan. No application fee.\nDuration: 30 September 2026 to 28 Februa
 ry 2027\, about 5 hours per week alongside your job.\n\nMore: https://fas.
 org/career/ai-safety-pef/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://fas.org/career/ai-safety-pef/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Primarily remote\, US-policy focused\, with two mandatory in-perso
 n events in the US (California retreat 4-7 November 2026\; Washington DC c
 apstone the week of 22 February 2027).
