UID:nieman-fellowship-class-of-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nieman Fellowships at Harvard\, Class of 2028
DESCRIPTION:The Nieman Foundation brings around two dozen journalists to Ha
 rvard each year for two semesters of study\, reflection and community\, on
 e of the oldest and best-known midcareer journalism fellowships in the wor
 ld. Fellows design their own course of study\, audit classes across Harvar
 d's schools and take part in Nieman's own seminars and master classes\; ma
 ny use the year to deepen a beat such as technology\, AI accountability\, 
 science or press freedom. WHAT YOU GET: a USD 87\,500 stipend paid over th
 e nine-month academic year (2026-27 figure)\, plus allowances toward housi
 ng\, childcare and health insurance. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: working journalists\
 , staff or freelance\, in any medium\, with at least five years of full-ti
 me media experience\; open to applicants from any country. Freelancers may
  use a recent supervising editor for one of the three required recommendat
 ion letters. Special fellowships within the program include the Nieman-Ber
 kman Klein Fellowship in Journalism Innovation. TO APPLY: applications for
  the class of 2028 open in the first week of October 2026 and require two 
 essays (personal statement and study proposal)\, work samples and three re
 commendation letters. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026 for international applican
 ts\; 31 January 2027 for US citizens.\n\nOrganisation: Nieman Foundation f
 or Journalism at Harvard\nLocation: Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, USA (resid
 ential academic year at Harvard)\nAward: USD 87\,500 stipend paid over the
  nine-month academic year (2026-27 figure)\, plus additional allowances fo
 r housing\, childcare and health insurance. Fellows audit courses across H
 arvard and participate in Nieman seminars\, master classes and workshops. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Two semesters in residence at Harvard\, aca
 demic year 2027-28\n\nMore: https://nieman.harvard.edu/fellowships/how-to-
 apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nieman.harvard.edu/fellowships/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, USA (residential academic year at Harv
 ard)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stigler-center-journalists-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261023T231835Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stigler Center: Journalists in Residence Program Spring 2
 027 (Chicago Booth)
DESCRIPTION:The Stigler Center at the University of Chicago Booth School of
  Business invites journalists from around the world to its Journalists in 
 Residence Program\, a roughly 12-week residency on the Hyde Park campus in
  spring 2027 focused on the interactions between politics\, business\, mar
 kets and the economy. Running since 2017\, the program has hosted journali
 sts from outlets including the BBC\, The New York Times and ABC News. WHAT
  YOU DO: audit three Chicago Booth classes\, participate actively in class
  discussions and complete required readings and assignments\, attend Stigl
 er Center seminars\, lectures\, conferences and other activities\, collabo
 rate with peers\, network with faculty and researchers\, and explore oppor
 tunities to write for the Center's ProMarket publication. WHAT YOU GET: US
 D 14\,000 stipend for living expenses\, economy-class airfare reimbursemen
 t\, SEVIS and visa application fee coverage\, health insurance through UCh
 icago\, housing guidance\, academic opportunities and a certificate upon c
 ompletion. Note that the stipend is subject to up to 14 percent tax withho
 lding for international participants and arrives after roughly the first m
 onth\, so you need funds to bridge that period. ELIGIBILITY: open to journ
 alists from all countries and media backgrounds\, including freelancers an
 d editors\, with some years of professional experience\, proficiency in En
 glish and a genuine interest in political economy and business reporting. 
 Successful applicants are notified by the end of December 2026. DEADLINE: 
 20 September 2026\, 11:59 pm Chicago time (CT).\n\nOrganisation: Stigler C
 enter\, University of Chicago Booth School of Business\nLocation: Universi
 ty of Chicago Booth School of Business\, Hyde Park campus\, Chicago\, USA.
  Open to journalists from all countries and media backgrounds.\nAward: USD
  14\,000 stipend to cover living expenses over the 12-week program\, plus 
 reimbursement of economy-class airfare to and from Chicago\, SEVIS and vis
 a application fees\, health insurance through UChicago\, and housing guida
 nce. The stipend is subject to up to 14 percent tax withholding for intern
 ational participants\, and you need sufficient funds for roughly the first
  month before the stipend arrives. No application fee.\nDuration: Approxim
 ately 12 weeks\, tentatively 15 March to 31 May 2027\n\nMore: https://www.
 chicagobooth.edu/research/stigler/education/journalists-in-residence-progr
 am?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.chicagobooth.edu/research/stigler/education/journalists-in-
 residence-program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
LOCATION:University of Chicago Booth School of Business\, Hyde Park campus\
 , Chicago\, USA. Open to journalists from all countries and media backgrou
 nds.
